<h2>Athens Gutter Questions We Get Asked</h2>

<h3>How much do seamless gutters cost in Athens, AL?</h3>

<p>Seamless gutter installation in Athens runs $8-15 per linear foot for 6-inch aluminum in .032 gauge. Most homes here need 150-200 linear feet, so a typical job lands between $1,200 and $3,000. Older homes with Victorian rooflines run higher — every extra corner is extra fabrication and extra labor. We measure the house before we quote rather than giving a range over the phone.</p>

<h3>Will gutter guards actually stop pine needles in Athens?</h3>

<p>Standard screens won't. Pine needles are thin enough to slip straight through and mat up inside the gutter. Micro-mesh guards designed for fine debris will. What guards do is reduce how often you clean — they don't eliminate it, and anyone telling you otherwise is selling. If you have multiple mature trees within twenty feet of your roofline, or pines anywhere in the yard, guards usually pay for themselves within a few years against the $150-300 a professional cleaning visit costs.</p>

<h3>Should I get 5-inch or 6-inch gutters in Athens?</h3>

<p>Six-inch, for most homes. It carries about 40% more water than 5-inch, and that matters twice over here: North Alabama gets 55-plus inches of rain a year, and a gutter carrying oak leaves and pine needles has less working capacity than its size suggests. The upgrade cost over 5-inch is small compared to what overflow does to a foundation.</p>

<h3>How long does seamless gutter installation take?</h3>

<p>Most Athens homes are a one-day job — four to six hours. We bring the roll-former to your driveway, fabricate each run on site, and hang as we go. Larger homes, complicated rooflines, or jobs that include rotten fascia repair can run into a second morning.</p>

<h3>Do you offer free estimates in Athens?</h3>

<p>Yes. Athens is about twenty-two miles from our office on Memorial Parkway in Huntsville, so we can usually get out within a day or two. We serve Athens, Tanner, Elkmont, Ardmore, and the rest of Limestone County. The estimate is free, in writing, and carries no obligation.</p>

